[{"id":2,"title":"KeyError when looking up a city that can't be found","kind":"bug","state":"open","labels":["bug"],"opened_by":"preethi-codes","opened_at":"2025-04-22","assigned_to":null,"body":"If you pass a city name that the API doesn't recognise, the whole program crashes with a KeyError instead of showing an error message.\n\n```\nKeyError: 'main'\n```\n\nI mistyped the city name and got this instead of a helpful message.\n\n**Steps to reproduce:**\n1. Call `parse_weather` with a response that has no `main` key (e.g. a 404 response from the API)\n2. Observe: unhandled KeyError, program exits\n\n**Expected:** A clean error message like \"City not found.\"\n**Actual:** Unhandled KeyError\n\n**Version:** 1.0.0\n**Python:** 3.12","comments":[{"author":"meera-writes-code","date":"2025-04-24","body":"Reproduced this too. Happens with any city name that returns a non-200 response."}],"lesson":"fix_pending_unmerged","lesson_feedback":"This bug is real and reproducible. But before you start: check the open PRs. Someone has already submitted a fix. It hasn't been merged — not because it's wrong, but because the maintainer hasn't responded to anything in over a year.","reproduction":{"issueId":"weatherly-2","buggyVersion":"1.0.0","fixedVersion":"1.1.0","reproductionSteps":[{"instruction":"Open weather.py and find the parse_weather function."},{"instruction":"Call parse_weather({'cod': '404', 'message': 'city not found'})"},{"instruction":"Observe what happens."}],"expectedResult":"parse_weather returns an error dict instead of crashing.","buggyBehavior":{"output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\n  File \"src/weather.py\", line 9, in parse_weather\n    temp = data[\"main\"][\"temp\"]\nKeyError: 'main'","type":"crash","verifiedByTest":true},"fixedBehavior":{"output":"{'error': 'Unexpected API response: missing weather data.'}","type":"validation_error","verifiedByTest":true},"regressionTestId":"weatherly/missing-main-key"}},{"id":5,"title":"Add option to display temperature in Fahrenheit","kind":"feature","state":"open","labels":["good first issue"],"opened_by":"kiran-weather-dev","opened_at":"2025-05-03","assigned_to":null,"body":"It would be useful to support a `--unit` flag so users can choose Celsius or Fahrenheit. The conversion is straightforward: `F = C * 9/5 + 32`.\n\nThis would be a good first contribution if anyone wants to pick it up.","comments":[{"author":"curious-dev","date":"2026-05-04","body":"Is anyone working on this? I'd be interested in picking it up."}],"lesson":"good_first_issue_hard","lesson_feedback":"The change itself is small, but consider the context before starting. Check the last commit date, the open PRs, and whether the maintainer has replied to anything recently.","reproduction":null},{"id":7,"title":"IndexError when API returns empty weather list","kind":"bug","state":"open","labels":["bug"],"opened_by":"infra-nerd-9","opened_at":"2025-05-05","assigned_to":null,"body":"Another crash in `parse_weather`. If the API returns a response where the `weather` array is empty, line `data['weather'][0]` raises an IndexError.\n\n```\nIndexError: list index out of range\n```\n\n**Steps to reproduce:**\n1. Call `parse_weather` with `{'main': {'temp': 18.0, 'humidity': 55}, 'weather': []}`\n2. Observe: IndexError\n\n**Expected:** A clean error message.\n**Actual:** Unhandled IndexError\n\n**Version:** 1.0.0\n**Python:** 3.12","comments":[{"author":"anon-contributor","date":"2025-11-20","body":"I'll take this one."},{"author":"random-dev-42","date":"2026-01-15","body":"Any progress on this? Still hitting the crash."}],"lesson":"claimed_never_started","lesson_feedback":"Someone claimed this over 10 months ago. No PR was ever opened. Before you start, leave a comment asking if they're still working on it — and also check the overall repo health before investing time here.","reproduction":{"issueId":"weatherly-7","buggyVersion":"1.0.0","fixedVersion":"1.1.0","reproductionSteps":[{"instruction":"Open weather.py and find the parse_weather function."},{"instruction":"Call parse_weather({'main': {'temp': 18.0, 'humidity': 55}, 'weather': []})"},{"instruction":"Observe what happens."}],"expectedResult":"parse_weather returns an error dict instead of crashing.","buggyBehavior":{"output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\n  File \"src/weather.py\", line 11, in parse_weather\n    description = data[\"weather\"][0][\"description\"]\nIndexError: list index out of range","type":"crash","verifiedByTest":true},"fixedBehavior":{"output":"{'error': 'Unexpected API response: weather list is empty.'}","type":"validation_error","verifiedByTest":true},"regressionTestId":"weatherly/empty-weather-list"}},{"id":20,"title":"API key invalid?","kind":"question","state":"open","labels":[],"opened_by":"frustrated-user-77","opened_at":"2026-02-28","assigned_to":null,"body":"Getting an error about invalid API key. Not sure what's happening. Can someone help?","comments":[],"lesson":"no_reproduction_steps","lesson_feedback":"No steps, no error message, no Python version, no indication of where they got their API key. There is not enough information here to help. The right move is to ask for the missing details — but also check whether the maintainer is likely to respond at all.","reproduction":null},{"id":22,"title":"Is this project still maintained?","kind":"question","state":"open","labels":[],"opened_by":"random-dev-42","opened_at":"2026-07-20","assigned_to":null,"body":"The last commit was over a year ago and open PRs are going unanswered. Is anyone still maintaining this? I'd like to contribute but I'm not sure it's worth the effort if nothing gets reviewed.","comments":[{"author":"anon-contributor","date":"2026-07-22","body":"I opened a PR 7 months ago and never heard back. I think it's safe to say it's abandoned."},{"author":"meera-writes-code","date":"2026-08-01","body":"Same experience here. Moving on to other projects."}],"lesson":"health_signal","lesson_feedback":"This is the clearest signal in the repo. Last commit 13+ months ago. Four open PRs, all unanswered. No maintainer reply anywhere. This is what an abandoned repo looks like. The right call is to walk away.","reproduction":null}]