[{"id":2,"title":"Add support for nested lists","state":"open","labels":["enhancement","good first issue"],"opened_by":"curious-dev","opened_at":"2026-03-10","assigned_to":null,"body":"It would be great if `render()` could handle nested lists. Right now only flat `- item` lists work. Indented items come out as paragraphs.\n\n```python\nrender('- item one\\n  - nested\\n- item two')\n# Expected: nested <ul> inside the outer <li>\n# Actual:   indented line becomes a <p>\n```\n\nWould love to see this supported.","comments":[{"author":"riya-dev","date":"2026-03-11","body":"Good first issue — extend the list handling in the block step. Happy to review."},{"author":"kai-dev","date":"2026-03-12","body":"Agreed, this comes up a lot. Would make the library a lot more practical."},{"author":"weekend-hacker","date":"2026-06-20","body":"I started looking at this. The list parser would need a full rewrite to track indentation state properly — pausing for now, it's more involved than I expected."}],"lesson":"good_first_issue_hard","lesson_feedback":"The maintainer called it a good first issue, but a contributor who tried it found the list parser needs a full rewrite. The block step doesn't track indentation state at all — adding nested support isn't an extension, it's a redesign. The difficulty is invisible until you read the code.","reproduction":{"issueId":"mdlite-2","buggyVersion":null,"fixedVersion":null,"reproductionSteps":[{"instruction":"Call render('- item one\\n  - nested\\n- item two')."},{"instruction":"Observe that the indented line is treated as a <p>, not a nested <li>."}],"expectedResult":"Nested list items render inside an inner <ul>.","buggyBehavior":{"output":"Indented list item becomes a <p> tag.","type":"wrong_output","verifiedByTest":false},"fixedBehavior":{"output":"N/A — no fix exists yet.","type":"success","verifiedByTest":false},"regressionTestId":null}},{"id":3,"title":"Double-underscore bold (__bold__) renders as plain text","state":"open","labels":["bug"],"opened_by":"priya-learns","opened_at":"2026-04-10","assigned_to":null,"body":"The README says both `**bold**` and `__bold__` should produce `<strong>`. But `__bold__` just passes through as plain text.\n\n```python\nrender('__bold__')\n# Returns: <p>__bold__</p>\n# Expected: <p><strong>bold</strong></p>\n```\n\n`**bold**` works fine. Only the double-underscore variant is broken.\n\n**Python:** 3.12","comments":[{"author":"riya-dev","date":"2026-04-10","body":"Confirmed. The `__` pattern is missing from `_inline` — only `**` is handled. Thanks for the report."},{"author":"kai-dev","date":"2026-04-11","body":"Reproduced on Python 3.11 as well."}],"lesson":"already_fixed_by_commit","lesson_feedback":"This issue is still open in the tracker but the bug no longer exists. Check the commits tab — the fix landed on 2026-04-22. Reproducing it on HEAD would have caught this immediately: __bold__ now renders correctly.","reproduction":{"issueId":"mdlite-3","buggyVersion":"pre-2026-04-22","fixedVersion":"HEAD","reproductionSteps":[{"instruction":"Open src/mdlite.py and find the _inline function."},{"instruction":"Call render('__bold__')."},{"instruction":"Check whether the output is <p>__bold__</p> or <p><strong>bold</strong></p>."}],"expectedResult":"render('__bold__') returns \"<p><strong>bold</strong></p>\"","buggyBehavior":{"output":"Returns \"<p>__bold__</p>\" — underscore bold not recognised.","type":"wrong_output","verifiedByTest":true},"fixedBehavior":{"output":"Returns \"<p><strong>bold</strong></p>\" — both bold variants work.","type":"success","verifiedByTest":true},"regressionTestId":"mdlite/bold-underscore"}},{"id":5,"title":"Raw HTML in input passes through into the output unchanged","state":"open","labels":["bug","good first issue"],"opened_by":"sec-minded-dev","opened_at":"2026-08-02","assigned_to":null,"body":"If you pass a string containing raw HTML to `render()`, it comes out unchanged inside a `<p>` tag.\n\n```python\nrender('<script>alert(1)</script>')\n# Returns: <p><script>alert(1)</script></p>\n```\n\nAny application that injects this output into a web page will execute the script. The library should escape `<`, `>`, and `&` before rendering.\n\n**Steps to reproduce:**\n1. Call `render('<script>alert(1)</script>')`\n2. Observe the output\n\n**Expected:** `<p>&lt;script&gt;alert(1)&lt;/script&gt;</p>`\n**Actual:** `<p><script>alert(1)</script></p>`\n\n**Python:** 3.12","comments":[{"author":"riya-dev","date":"2026-08-03","body":"Confirmed. The fix goes in `_inline` — call `html.escape(text)` at the very top, before any of the regex patterns run. Please include a test that fails on the current code and passes after your fix."},{"author":"kai-dev","date":"2026-08-04","body":"Reproduced on Python 3.12 as well. The escape needs to happen before the regexes or the `&` in `&lt;` will get double-processed."}],"lesson":"genuine_good_pick","lesson_feedback":"Good pick. Clear reproduction steps, confirmed by two maintainers, fix location spelled out in the comments, no PR exists, and the scope is a single line in _inline. This is exactly the kind of issue worth starting with.","reproduction":{"issueId":"mdlite-5","buggyVersion":"HEAD","fixedVersion":"fixed","reproductionSteps":[{"instruction":"Open src/mdlite.py and find the _inline function."},{"instruction":"Call render('<script>alert(1)</script>')."},{"instruction":"Observe the return value."}],"expectedResult":"render returns \"<p>&lt;script&gt;alert(1)&lt;/script&gt;</p>\"","buggyBehavior":{"output":"Returns \"<p><script>alert(1)</script></p>\" — raw HTML passes through unchanged.","type":"wrong_output","verifiedByTest":true},"fixedBehavior":{"output":"Returns \"<p>&lt;script&gt;alert(1)&lt;/script&gt;</p>\" — HTML characters are safely escaped.","type":"success","verifiedByTest":true},"regressionTestId":"mdlite/raw-html-passthrough"}},{"id":6,"title":"Links break sometimes","state":"open","labels":["bug"],"opened_by":"confused-first-timer","opened_at":"2026-08-20","assigned_to":null,"body":"Sometimes when I use links in my markdown the output doesn't look right. Not sure what's happening.\n\nI'm using Python 3.11.","comments":[{"author":"riya-dev","date":"2026-08-21","body":"Hi, thanks for the report. Could you share the exact markdown string you're passing in and the output you're getting? A short code snippet like `render('[text](url)')` and what it returns would help a lot."},{"author":"confused-first-timer","date":"2026-08-23","body":"It's all in a large file, I can't really paste it all here. The output just looks wrong in some cases."}],"lesson":"no_reproduction_steps","lesson_feedback":"No input, no output, no specific case. The maintainer asked for a code snippet two days after the report and the response was 'it's in a large file'. You cannot reproduce this, which means you cannot fix it. The right move is to wait for a proper example — or ask for one yourself.","reproduction":{"issueId":"mdlite-6","buggyVersion":null,"fixedVersion":null,"reproductionSteps":[{"instruction":"Read the issue body carefully."},{"instruction":"Check whether a specific markdown input is provided."},{"instruction":"Check whether the actual vs expected output is shown."}],"expectedResult":"A reproducible code snippet showing the exact input and the wrong output.","buggyBehavior":{"output":"Not enough information to reproduce. No input string or output provided.","type":"wrong_output","verifiedByTest":false},"fixedBehavior":{"output":"N/A — cannot investigate without a reproduction case.","type":"success","verifiedByTest":false},"regressionTestId":null}},{"id":8,"title":"README example has a typo in the function call","state":"open","labels":["docs"],"opened_by":"weekend-hacker","opened_at":"2026-09-05","assigned_to":null,"body":"The usage example in README.md has a typo in the function call — it says `form` instead of `from`.\n\n```\nform src.mdlite import render\n```\n\nShould be:\n\n```\nfrom src.mdlite import render\n```\n\nSmall fix but confusing for new users.","comments":[{"author":"riya-dev","date":"2026-09-06","body":"Good catch, typo fixes are welcome. Please use a `docs/` branch, e.g. `docs/readme-typo`."},{"author":"priya-learns","date":"2026-09-11","body":"I'll fix this."}],"lesson":"claimed_active_pr","lesson_feedback":"A contributor has already claimed this and opened a draft PR (#9) on 2026-09-12. Starting on this without checking first would duplicate their work. Leave a comment asking for an update, or look for another issue.","reproduction":{"issueId":"mdlite-8","buggyVersion":null,"fixedVersion":null,"reproductionSteps":[{"instruction":"Open README.md and find the usage example."},{"instruction":"Check the import line."}],"expectedResult":"Import line reads: from src.mdlite import render","buggyBehavior":{"output":"Import line reads: form src.mdlite import render — typo in README.","type":"wrong_output","verifiedByTest":false},"fixedBehavior":{"output":"Import line reads: from src.mdlite import render","type":"success","verifiedByTest":false},"regressionTestId":null}}]